    "The exposure counts are roughly balanced across the ten classes, which is desirable for a MaxDiff design.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "## Counts Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "The counts analysis is the simplest way to summarize MaxDiff results. For each class, I calculate the percentage of times it was selected as best and the percentage of times it was selected as worst. The score is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{score}_j = \\%\\text{best}_j - \\%\\text{worst}_j\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "A high positive score means the class was frequently selected as best. A negative score means the class was more often selected as worst."
   ]
  },
