    "The bootstrap confidence intervals provide a measure of uncertainty around the counts scores. Marketing Analytics remains the strongest performer even after accounting for sampling variability, with a confidence interval that remains well above zero. Business Analytics and Customer Analytics also show consistently positive scores.\n",
    "\n",
    "In contrast, Analytics Consulting has a confidence interval that lies almost entirely below zero, suggesting that it is consistently among the least preferred classes. Classes near the middle of the ranking have wider overlap in their confidence intervals, indicating greater uncertainty and making small ranking differences less meaningful.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "## From MaxDiff Data to MNL Choices\n",
    "\n",
    "The MaxDiff survey can be converted into multinomial logit (MNL) choice observations. Each survey task provides two separate choices.\n",
    "\n",
    "First, the respondent selects the most preferred item from the four classes shown on the screen. This creates a standard multinomial logit choice among four alternatives.\n",
    "\n",
    "Second, after removing the selected best item, the respondent chooses the least preferred item from the remaining three alternatives. Following the approach discussed in class, the worst choice is modeled as a best choice among the remaining alternatives with utilities multiplied by -1.\n",
    "\n",
    "The MNL model assigns each class a utility coefficient $\\beta_j$. For a task showing items $\\{a,b,c,d\\}$, the probability that item $b$ is selected as best is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P(\\text{best}=b)\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{\\exp(\\beta_b)}\n",
    "{\\exp(\\beta_a)+\\exp(\\beta_b)+\\exp(\\beta_c)+\\exp(\\beta_d)}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "After removing the best item, the probability that item $c$ is selected as worst is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P(\\text{worst}=c \\mid \\text{best}=b)\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{\\exp(-\\beta_c)}\n",
    "{\\exp(-\\beta_a)+\\exp(-\\beta_c)+\\exp(-\\beta_d)}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Because adding the same constant to every utility does not change the probabilities, the model is not fully identified. Therefore, one coefficient must be fixed as a reference level. I set:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\beta_1 = 0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "and estimate the remaining nine coefficients.\n",
    "\n",
    "Before fitting the MNL model, I first verify that every task contains exactly:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Four items shown\n",
    "- One best choice\n",
    "- One worst choice\n",
    "\n",
    "Any incomplete or invalid tasks are removed before estimation."
