   "source": [
    "The counts ranking and MNL ranking are expected to be broadly similar. Differences may occur because the MNL model accounts for which classes were shown together in each task, while the counts analysis only considers the frequency of best and worst selections.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "## MNL via Bayesian Estimation\n",
    "\n",
    "The Bayesian MNL model uses the same likelihood as the maximum likelihood model but combines it with a prior distribution on the utility coefficients.\n",
    "\n",
    "Using Bayes' rule, the posterior distribution is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\pi(\\boldsymbol{\\beta}\\mid \\boldsymbol{y})\n",
    "\\propto\n",
    "L(\\boldsymbol{\\beta})\n",
    "\\cdot\n",
    "\\pi(\\boldsymbol{\\beta})\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- \\(L(\\boldsymbol{\\beta})\\) is the MNL likelihood\n",
    "- \\(\\pi(\\boldsymbol{\\beta})\\) is the prior distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "I use a weakly informative normal prior:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\beta_j \\sim N(0,10)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This prior is intentionally broad so that the observed data dominate the estimation.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Posterior Function"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "6462e8d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def log_prior(beta_free):\n",
    "\n",
    "    return np.sum(\n",
    "        -0.5 * np.log(2 * np.pi * 10)\n",
    "        - (beta_free ** 2) / (2 * 10)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "def log_posterior(beta_free, task_data):\n",
    "\n",
    "    return (\n",
    "        log_likelihood(beta_free, task_data)\n",
    "        +\n",
    "        log_prior(beta_free)\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "74a5ff11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Metropolis-Hastings Sampler\n",
    "\n",
    "I use a random-walk Metropolis-Hastings sampler. At each iteration, the algorithm proposes a new parameter vector and decides whether to accept or reject it based on the posterior density."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "48aa961c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def mh_sampler(beta0, n_iter, step, task_data):\n",
    "\n",
    "    K = len(beta0)\n",
    "\n",
    "    draws = np.zeros((n_iter, K))\n",
    "\n",
    "    beta = beta0.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    lp = log_posterior(beta, task_data)\n",
    "\n",
    "    accept = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "    for t in range(n_iter):\n",
    "\n",
    "        beta_star = (\n",
    "            beta\n",
    "            +\n",
    "            np.random.normal(\n",
    "                0,\n",
    "                step,\n",
    "                size=K\n",
    "            )\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        lp_star = log_posterior(\n",
    "            beta_star,\n",
    "            task_data\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        if np.log(np.random.rand()) < (lp_star - lp):\n",
    "\n",
    "            beta = beta_star\n",
    "            lp = lp_star\n",
    "            accept += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "        draws[t] = beta\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"draws\": draws,\n",
    "        \"accept_rate\": accept / n_iter\n",
    "    }"
   ]
  },
