  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "394d89fe",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The trace plots exhibit stable fluctuations around a constant mean with no visible upward or downward trend. The chains appear to have mixed well after burn-in, suggesting that the Metropolis-Hastings sampler reached a stationary distribution and produced reliable posterior draws.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Posterior Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "After removing the burn-in period, I summarize the posterior distribution of the utility coefficients. Specifically, I calculate the posterior mean and the 95% credible interval for each class using the retained MCMC draws. These summaries will later be used to compare class preferences and quantify estimation uncertainty."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "4ee72927",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "draws_full = np.column_stack([\n",
    "    np.zeros(draws_post.shape[0]),\n",
    "    draws_post\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "post_mean_beta = (\n",
    "    draws_full.mean(axis=0)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "post_ci_low = (\n",
    "    np.quantile(\n",
    "        draws_full,\n",
    "        0.025,\n",
    "        axis=0\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "post_ci_high = (\n",
    "    np.quantile(\n",
    "        draws_full,\n",
    "        0.975,\n",
    "        axis=0\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5bc279f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Posterior Shares of Preference\n",
    "\n",
    "For each posterior draw, the utility coefficients are converted into preference shares:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat{s}_j^{(s)}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{\\exp(\\hat{\\beta}_j^{(s)})}\n",
    "{\\sum_k \\exp(\\hat{\\beta}_k^{(s)})}\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "id": "c6bdad99",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "share_draws = np.exp(draws_full)\n",
    "\n",
    "share_draws = (\n",
    "    share_draws\n",
    "    /\n",
    "    share_draws.sum(\n",
    "        axis=1,\n",
    "        keepdims=True\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "post_mean_share = (\n",
    "    share_draws.mean(axis=0)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "share_ci_low = (\n",
    "    np.quantile(\n",
    "        share_draws,\n",
    "        0.025,\n",
    "        axis=0\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "share_ci_high = (\n",
    "    np.quantile(\n",
    "        share_draws,\n",
    "        0.975,\n",
    "        axis=0\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
